@startuml Kong Gateway - Detailed Sequence Diagram

!theme plain
title Kong API Gateway - Request Processing Flow (Local Development)

actor User
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant "Kong Gateway\n:8000" as Kong
participant "JWT Plugin" as JWT
participant "JWT Claims\nHeaders Plugin" as Claims
participant "API Gateway\nSecret Plugin" as Secret
participant "Auth Service\n:3001" as Auth
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== User Request ==

User -> Browser: Click "View Profile"
Browser -> Kong: GET /api/auth/profile\nAuthorization: Bearer eyJhbGc...

== Kong Processing ==

Kong -> Kong: Match route
note right
    Path: /api/auth/profile
    Matched: auth-protected-route
    Service: auth-service
end note

Kong -> JWT: Execute Plugin\n(Priority: 1000)

JWT -> JWT: Extract JWT from header
note right
    Authorization: Bearer <token>
    → token = eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIs...
end note

JWT -> JWT: Verify JWT Signature
note right
    Algorithm: RS256
    Public Key: ENV variable
    
    ✅ Signature valid
end note

JWT -> JWT: Verify Claims
note right
    Check expiration:
    exp: 1735574400 (timestamp)
    now: 1735570800
    
    ✅ Not expired (exp > now)
end note

JWT -> Kong: Store token in context
note right
    kong.ctx.shared.authenticated_jwt_token = <token>
end note

Kong -> Claims: Execute Plugin\n(Priority: 1000)

Claims -> Claims: Get token from context
note right
    jwt_token = kong.ctx.shared.authenticated_jwt_token
end note

Claims -> Claims: Decode JWT payload
note right
    JWT structure:
    header.payload.signature
    
    Extract part 2 (payload):
    eyJpZCI6IjUwN2Yx...
    
    Base64 decode:
    {
      "id": "507f1f77bcf86cd799439011",
      "email": "john@example.com",
      "role": "user",
      "full_name": "John Doe",
      "iss": "auth-service",
      "exp": 1735574400
    }
end note

Claims -> Claims: Extract configured claims
note right
    claims_to_include:
    - id
    - email
    - role
    - full_name
end note

Claims -> Kong: Add headers to request
note right
    x-user-id: 507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
    x-user-email: john@example.com
    x-user-role: user
    x-user-full_name: John Doe
end note

Kong -> Secret: Execute Plugin\n(Priority: 1100)

Secret -> Kong: Add secret header
note right
    x-api-gateway-secret: test-secret-e2e
end note

== Forward to Service ==

Kong -> Auth: Proxied Request
note right
    GET http://auth-service:3001/api/auth/profile
    
    Headers:
    - x-user-id: 507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
    - x-user-email: john@example.com
    - x-user-role: user
    - x-user-full_name: John Doe
    - x-api-gateway-secret: test-secret-e2e
end note

== Service Processing ==

Auth -> Auth: validateApiGatewaySecret
note right
    const secret = req.headers['x-api-gateway-secret'];
    
    if (secret === process.env.API_GATEWAY_SECRET) {
        ✅ Valid - request from Kong
    } else {
        ❌ 403 Forbidden
    }
end note

Auth -> Auth: Extract user info
note right
    const userId = req.headers['x-user-id'];
    const email = req.headers['x-user-email'];
    const role = req.headers['x-user-role'];
    
    ✅ No JWT verification needed!
    ✅ Kong already validated
end note

Auth -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE id = '507f1f77bcf86cd799439011'

DB -> Auth: User data

Auth -> Auth: Build response
note right
    {
      "id": "507f1f77bcf86cd799439011",
      "email": "john@example.com",
      "full_name": "John Doe",
      "role": "user",
      "created_at": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    }
end note

== Response ==

Auth -> Kong: 200 OK\n+ User Profile JSON

Kong -> Browser: 200 OK\n+ User Profile JSON

Browser -> User: Display Profile

== Timing ==

note over Kong, Auth
    **Performance Breakdown:**
    
    1. Route Matching: ~2ms
    2. JWT Plugin (verify): ~15ms
    3. Claims Plugin (extract): ~5ms
    4. Secret Plugin (add header): ~1ms
    5. Proxy to service: ~2ms
    6. Service processing: ~20ms
    
    **Total: ~45ms**
    
    **Benefits:**
    • JWT verified once at gateway
    • Services don't need JWT libraries
    • Consistent security policy
    • Easy to audit/monitor
end note

@enduml
